{
  "video": {
    "id": "R_8beV_gXHc",
    "title": "Exploration of the Amplitude and Phase: Second Order II Applet",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R_8beV_gXHc",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 708,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 284,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 2.87,
      "end": 2.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Welcome to the applet amplitude and"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 2.88,
      "end": 6.23,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "phase second order two."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 6.24,
      "end": 8.67,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "This applet is a sibling of the applet"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 8.68,
      "end": 11.19,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "amplitude and phase first order, which I"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 11.2,
      "end": 13.15,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "used to introduce the MIT Mathlet"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 13.16,
      "end": 16.07,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "Collection. Its color coding, placement"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 16.08,
      "end": 18.43,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "conventions, and its functionalities are"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 18.44,
      "end": 20.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "identical to that one."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 20.72,
      "end": 22.43,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "This applet represents a mechanical"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 22.44,
      "end": 24.63,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "system driven"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 24.64,
      "end": 27.35,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "by the motion of the far end of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 27.36,
      "end": 29.27,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "dashpot."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 29.28,
      "end": 32.31,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "Let's begin by animating the system to"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 32.32,
      "end": 34.39,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "see how this works."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 34.4,
      "end": 36.23,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "You can see the dashpot is moving up and"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 36.24,
      "end": 39.39,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "down sinusoidally, driving a mass in"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 39.4,
      "end": 42.03,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "yellow, and the mass is also constrained"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 42.04,
      "end": 44.55,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "by a spring at the top attached to a"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 44.56,
      "end": 46.99,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "fixed wall at the top. Perhaps we should"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 48.83,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "animate this again so you can see the"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 48.84,
      "end": 53.11,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "whole thing at work."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 55.91,
      "end": 55.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "This applet and its siblings"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 55.92,
      "end": 58.63,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "show only the steady-state or periodic"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 58.64,
      "end": 61.07,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "solutions to these equations. They don't"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 61.08,
      "end": 63.31,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "allow you to pick initial conditions."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 63.32,
      "end": 65.03,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "They don't represent the effect of"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 65.04,
      "end": 67.51,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "transients."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 67.52,
      "end": 70.67,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "In the applet, X represents the position"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 70.68,
      "end": 72.83,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "of the mass, and you can see it read off"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 72.84,
      "end": 74.35,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "on this scale."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 74.36,
      "end": 76.91,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "It's represented in yellow on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 76.92,
      "end": 79.95,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "graphing window here."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 79.96,
      "end": 84.59,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "And we declare X to be zero when the"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 84.6,
      "end": 89.11,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "text": "spring is ex- exerting no force on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 89.12,
      "end": 92.47,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "mass. It's at rest."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 92.48,
      "end": 94.71,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "We declare X to be the output signal of"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 94.72,
      "end": 96.47,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 96.48,
      "end": 99.39,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "In the Mathlet, Y denotes the position"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 99.4,
      "end": 101.35,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "of the plunger, and it's read off by"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 101.36,
      "end": 104.07,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "this scale here."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 104.08,
      "end": 106.83,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "We declare Y to be the input signal of"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 106.84,
      "end": 108.59,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 108.6,
      "end": 110.87,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "Now, the force exerted by a dashpot is"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 110.88,
      "end": 113.07,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "proportional to the relative velocity of"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 113.08,
      "end": 115.55,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "the cylinder and the piston sliding"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 115.56,
      "end": 116.99,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "inside of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 117.0,
      "end": 118.95,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "The proportionality constant is called"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 118.96,
      "end": 120.19,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "B."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 120.2,
      "end": 122.35,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "As a consequence,"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 122.36,
      "end": 123.99,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "the right-hand side of the equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 124.0,
      "end": 125.99,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "controlling the position of the mass is"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 126.0,
      "end": 129.43,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "B Y dot, B times the time derivative of"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 129.44,
      "end": 130.59,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "Y."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 130.6,
      "end": 132.07,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "This is a good example in which the"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 132.08,
      "end": 134.07,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "right-hand side of a linear equation in"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 134.08,
      "end": 136.55,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "standard form is not just the input"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 136.56,
      "end": 138.87,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "signal. In this case, it's not even a"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 138.88,
      "end": 141.15,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "multiple of the input signal. It's a"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 141.16,
      "end": 142.95,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "multiple of the derivative of the input"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 142.96,
      "end": 145.07,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "signal."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 145.08,
      "end": 146.87,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "The most important case to study is that"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 146.88,
      "end": 148.87,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "in which the input signal is sinusoidal,"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 148.88,
      "end": 151.43,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "and that's what is represented here."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 151.44,
      "end": 153.19,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "In the applet, we take the amplitude of"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 153.2,
      "end": 155.67,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "the input signal to be one."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 155.68,
      "end": 157.75,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "If the amplitude of the input signal is"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 157.76,
      "end": 160.27,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "doubled, so is the its derivative, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 160.28,
      "end": 162.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "so by superposition, the amplitude of"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 162.36,
      "end": 164.91,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "the output signal would also be doubled."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 164.92,
      "end": 167.23,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "So, setting the input's amplitude equal"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 167.24,
      "end": 171.23,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "to one isn't really a restriction."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 171.24,
      "end": 173.19,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "In this situation, when the input"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 173.2,
      "end": 176.47,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "amplitude is one, the output amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 176.48,
      "end": 180.63,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "is the same as the gain of the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 180.64,
      "end": 182.67,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "We can see how this output amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 182.68,
      "end": 185.15,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "depends upon the input frequency by"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 185.16,
      "end": 188.75,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "opening the Bode plot window here."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 188.76,
      "end": 191.51,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "This opens two windows. The top one"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 191.52,
      "end": 195.11,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "represents the amplitude of the system"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 195.12,
      "end": 198.47,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "response, the gain, as a function of"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 198.48,
      "end": 201.55,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "omega, and we can start with omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 201.56,
      "end": 204.15,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "small. When omega equals zero, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 204.16,
      "end": 206.39,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "plunger isn't moving at all,"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 206.4,
      "end": 207.59,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "and"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 207.6,
      "end": 210.51,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "the mass has no reason to move either,"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 210.52,
      "end": 213.15,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "so it's at the X equals zero, the spring"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 213.16,
      "end": 216.87,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "is relaxed, there's no motion."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 216.88,
      "end": 219.31,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "When omega increases, the system"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 219.32,
      "end": 222.19,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "response is becomes"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 222.2,
      "end": 223.43,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "greater,"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 223.44,
      "end": 225.19,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "but you'll notice something interesting"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 225.2,
      "end": 226.63,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "in this system,"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 226.64,
      "end": 229.15,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "when omega is small, the system response"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 229.16,
      "end": 232.11,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "leads the input signal."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 232.12,
      "end": 235.35,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "That is to say, the phase lag is"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 235.36,
      "end": 238.27,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "negative, and that's represented here."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 238.28,
      "end": 239.95,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "This is a little confusing. This is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 239.96,
      "end": 242.59,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "graph of the negative of the phase lag,"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 242.6,
      "end": 246.59,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "or the phase gain, and that's a positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 246.6,
      "end": 250.47,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "angle in this in this uh system for"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 250.48,
      "end": 252.95,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "omega small."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 252.96,
      "end": 255.99,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "You can see the effect the mass seems to"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 256.0,
      "end": 258.11,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "be pulling the plunger, although that's"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 258.12,
      "end": 260.509,
      "duration": 2.389,
      "text": "not actually what's happening."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 260.519,
      "end": 262.39,
      "duration": 1.871,
      "text": "When omega increases,"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 262.4,
      "end": 263.87,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "the the"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 263.88,
      "end": 265.67,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "amplitude of the system response"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 265.68,
      "end": 266.95,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "increases"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 266.96,
      "end": 270.71,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "until a critical moment when"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 270.72,
      "end": 273.83,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "omega takes on some critical value. This"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 273.84,
      "end": 277.03,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "is the resonant frequency of the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 277.04,
      "end": 279.11,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "And at this point, the system response"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 279.12,
      "end": 281.67,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "is identical to the input signal."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 281.68,
      "end": 283.07,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "Shall we see what this looks like by"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 283.08,
      "end": 285.59,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "animating the system?"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 285.6,
      "end": 288.83,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "And now, the plunger seems to be locked"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 288.84,
      "end": 290.79,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "to the piston. That's not actually the"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 290.8,
      "end": 294.11,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "case, but the system is simply operating"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 294.12,
      "end": 296.47,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "in harmony here. Uh it's the resonant"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 296.48,
      "end": 298.39,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "frequency."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 298.4,
      "end": 300.91,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "When omega increases still further,"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 300.92,
      "end": 304.67,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "then the system response falls off, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 304.68,
      "end": 306.99,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "phase lag becomes positive, the response"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 307.0,
      "end": 310.63,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "falls behind the input signal."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 310.64,
      "end": 312.83,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "And that's quite That's all visible from"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 312.84,
      "end": 314.59,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "the Bode plot pictures."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 314.6,
      "end": 316.59,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "You know, as I look at this, I notice"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 316.6,
      "end": 318.99,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "something interesting."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 319.0,
      "end": 320.47,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "The"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 320.48,
      "end": 324.03,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "when the amplitude when the system"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 324.04,
      "end": 328.35,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "response reaches a maximum or a minimum,"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 328.36,
      "end": 330.95,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "that's exactly the same moment as when"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 330.96,
      "end": 334.59,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "the system response curve crosses the"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 334.6,
      "end": 337.43,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "input signal curve. So, the the In other"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 337.44,
      "end": 339.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "words, the amplitude of the output"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 339.72,
      "end": 340.79,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "signal"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 340.8,
      "end": 344.31,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "equals the value of the input signal at"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 344.32,
      "end": 346.39,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "the moment when they cross."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 346.4,
      "end": 348.47,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "Let's see if that is always the case."
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 348.48,
      "end": 350.55,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "When I change the frequency here, that"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 350.56,
      "end": 353.11,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "always seems to be the case."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 353.12,
      "end": 355.35,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "Very interesting."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 355.36,
      "end": 357.75,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And in fact, perhaps we should change"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 357.76,
      "end": 360.63,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "the values of B and K"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 360.64,
      "end": 362.19,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "to see whether that continues to be the"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 362.2,
      "end": 363.19,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "case."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 363.2,
      "end": 365.19,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "Yes, it just seems to drag up and down"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 365.2,
      "end": 367.31,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "there."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 367.32,
      "end": 370.03,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "And similarly, if I change the value of"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 370.04,
      "end": 372.99,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "the spring constant K, again, that peak"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 373.0,
      "end": 375.27,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "seems to move up and down along the blue"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 375.28,
      "end": 376.87,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "curve. Very odd. We'll come back to"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 376.88,
      "end": 378.67,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "that."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 378.68,
      "end": 380.19,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "Here are some further"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 380.2,
      "end": 382.59,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "observations that you can see from"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 382.6,
      "end": 385.51,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "experimenting with this applet."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 385.52,
      "end": 386.83,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "First of all,"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 386.84,
      "end": 388.79,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "let's watch what happens if I change the"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 388.8,
      "end": 391.83,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "value of the damping constant B."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 391.84,
      "end": 394.27,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "I'm going to watch the Bode plot over"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 394.28,
      "end": 397.91,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "here, the amplitude Bode plot."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 400.23,
      "end": 400.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Well, it changes, but one thing that"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 400.24,
      "end": 402.31,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "doesn't change is the position of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 402.32,
      "end": 404.71,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "resonant peak there."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 404.72,
      "end": 406.43,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "In other words, the resonant frequency"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 406.44,
      "end": 409.15,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "seems to be independent of the value of"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 409.16,
      "end": 412.47,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "B, of the damping constant."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 412.48,
      "end": 415.35,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "Second thing you can observe as I vary B"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 415.36,
      "end": 417.75,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "is, well, when B is large, the resonant"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 417.76,
      "end": 420.47,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "hump is quite broad, but when B becomes"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 420.48,
      "end": 423.23,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "small, as B becomes smaller, that spike"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 423.24,
      "end": 425.11,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "becomes narrower and narrower and"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 425.12,
      "end": 427.63,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "narrower."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 427.64,
      "end": 429.27,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "And the third thing you can notice from"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 429.28,
      "end": 431.75,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "looking at this is, as B gets to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 431.76,
      "end": 435.71,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "small, the flip between uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 435.72,
      "end": 439.51,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "phase lag of close to minus pi over two"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 439.52,
      "end": 442.67,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "to a phase lag of close to plus pi over"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 442.68,
      "end": 445.99,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "two happens more and more abruptly as I"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 446.0,
      "end": 449.15,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "change the frequency from something"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 449.16,
      "end": 452.11,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "small and cross through that resonant"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 452.12,
      "end": 453.75,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "peak."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 453.76,
      "end": 456.19,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "Now, the system response is ahead of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 456.2,
      "end": 459.35,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "input signal, but it very quickly flips"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 459.36,
      "end": 461.91,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "to being behind it uh as you cross the"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 461.92,
      "end": 464.03,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "resonant frequency, and that transition"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 464.04,
      "end": 466.63,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "happens more and more rapidly as B gets"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 466.64,
      "end": 468.43,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "to be small."
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 468.44,
      "end": 470.23,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "Each one of these three observations can"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 470.24,
      "end": 471.07,
      "duration": 0.83,
      "text": "be"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 471.08,
      "end": 474.59,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "verified by calculation."
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 474.6,
      "end": 476.83,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "The relationship between the gain"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 476.84,
      "end": 479.95,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "and the phase lag can be uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 479.96,
      "end": 481.79,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "uh illustrated very well using the"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 481.8,
      "end": 484.23,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "Nyquist plot, which I'll open using this"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 484.24,
      "end": 487.19,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "key."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 489.67,
      "end": 489.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "This is a plot of the complex plane,"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 489.68,
      "end": 493.59,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "and on it is drawn a complex number in"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 493.6,
      "end": 494.79,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "yellow,"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 494.8,
      "end": 498.15,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "and that complex number"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 498.16,
      "end": 500.47,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "uh has an has a"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 500.48,
      "end": 501.99,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "a magnitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 502.0,
      "end": 504.03,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "and an angle."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 504.04,
      "end": 505.59,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "The magnitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 505.6,
      "end": 508.79,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "is the pha- is the gain."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 508.8,
      "end": 511.87,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "It This yellow strut is the same just"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 511.88,
      "end": 515.67,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "length as this radius vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 515.68,
      "end": 520.029,
      "duration": 4.349,
      "text": "And the angle is the negative of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 520.039,
      "end": 522.63,
      "duration": 2.591,
      "text": "phase lag. It's the phase gain. So, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 522.64,
      "end": 524.59,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "angle is positive here, it goes through"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 524.6,
      "end": 525.71,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 525.72,
      "end": 526.79,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "here,"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 526.8,
      "end": 529.47,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "and becomes negative down here when the"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 529.48,
      "end": 531.59,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "phase lag becomes positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 531.6,
      "end": 533.79,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "So, you can see the relationship between"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 533.8,
      "end": 537.87,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "You can see why it is that the um"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 537.88,
      "end": 540.51,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "resonant peak occurs at exactly the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 540.52,
      "end": 542.91,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "instant as when the phase lag is zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 542.92,
      "end": 544.83,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "That says that"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 544.84,
      "end": 548.75,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "this trajectory, this Nyquist plot,"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 548.76,
      "end": 550.31,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "goes through this point, which is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 550.32,
      "end": 553.71,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "point one in the complex plane,"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 553.72,
      "end": 555.15,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "where the angle is zero and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 555.16,
      "end": 557.79,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "magnitude is one."
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 557.8,
      "end": 560.15,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "This trajectory is, in fact, independent"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 560.16,
      "end": 562.87,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "of each either both of the system"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 562.88,
      "end": 567.15,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "parameters. If I change them,"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 567.16,
      "end": 569.39,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "many things change, but the shape of"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 569.4,
      "end": 571.51,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "this trajectory, the Nyquist plot, is"
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 571.52,
      "end": 573.19,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "independent of those two system"
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 573.2,
      "end": 576.63,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "parameters. And in fact, it's a circle"
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 576.64,
      "end": 579.43,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "of radius one half and center one half."
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 579.44,
      "end": 581.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "You can verify that by calculation as"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 581.72,
      "end": 583.51,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "well."
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 583.52,
      "end": 586.87,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "That fact explains the observation we"
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 586.88,
      "end": 589.55,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "made earlier, that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 589.56,
      "end": 592.99,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "mac- amplitude of the system response,"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 593.0,
      "end": 594.31,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "the gain,"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 594.32,
      "end": 599.75,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "seems to equal the value of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 599.76,
      "end": 602.15,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "input signal"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 602.16,
      "end": 605.35,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "when that maximum is achieved. In other"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 605.36,
      "end": 609.63,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "words, the claim is that the gain equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 609.64,
      "end": 611.43,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "the cosine"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 611.44,
      "end": 612.55,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "of"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 612.56,
      "end": 616.71,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "the phase lag."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 616.72,
      "end": 622.31,
      "duration": 5.59,
      "text": "The gain is the cosine of the phase lag."
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 626.31,
      "end": 626.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "This curve is given by the equation the"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 626.32,
      "end": 627.83,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "radius"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 627.84,
      "end": 629.19,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 629.2,
      "end": 632.27,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "the cosine of the angle."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 632.28,
      "end": 634.59,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "R equals cosine theta is a polar"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 634.6,
      "end": 637.55,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "equation for this particular circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 637.56,
      "end": 639.75,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "And so the fact that this is a circle is"
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 639.76,
      "end": 642.31,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "the same as the fact that we observed"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 642.32,
      "end": 643.39,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "earlier"
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 643.4,
      "end": 647.59,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "that the solution curve crosses the"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 647.6,
      "end": 649.91,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "input curve just when it reaches a"
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 649.92,
      "end": 653.71,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "maximum or a minimum."
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 655.47,
      "end": 655.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Well, in addition to the spring system"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 655.48,
      "end": 657.55,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "shown in this applet, this very same"
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 657.56,
      "end": 659.47,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "equation models the response of an AM"
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 659.48,
      "end": 661.11,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "radio receiver."
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 661.12,
      "end": 663.03,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "The input signal is the incoming radio"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 663.04,
      "end": 665.19,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "signal which contains electromagnetic"
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 665.2,
      "end": 666.63,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "magnetic waves of many different"
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 666.64,
      "end": 667.87,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "frequencies."
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 667.88,
      "end": 669.31,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "The output signal feeds to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 669.32,
